==English==

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|fro|estraction}}, from {{der|en|ML.|extractio}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɪkˈstɹækʃən/}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-extraction.wav|Audio (UK)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ækʃən}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# An act of [[extracting]] or the condition of being [[extracted]].
# A person's [[origin]] or [[ancestry]].
#* '''2014''', Larissa Remennick, ''Russian Israelis: Social Mobility, Politics and Culture'', Routledge {{ISBN|9781317977698}}, page 144
#*: Our companion on these tours was a young tourist, an American of Russian '''extraction''', whose questions and remarks drew our attention to some details of Haifa life that have become too familiar and would have otherwise passed unnoticed.&nbsp;...
# Something extracted, an [[extract]], as from a [[plant]] or an organ of an animal etc.
#* {{RQ:Milton Areo|passage=They [books] do preserve as in a vial the purest efficacy and '''extraction''' of that living intellect that bred them.}}
# {{lb|en|military}} An act of removing someone from a hostile area to a secure location.
# {{lb|en|dentistry}} A removal of a [[tooth]] from its [[socket]].

